# stayAwakeBot / `saw`

Read `AGENTS.md` (same text as `CLAUDE.md`) and the matching skill in `.cursor/skills/` before
non-trivial work. Skills publish **obligations**, never detection mechanisms.

1. **Zero downgrade.** Detection/perf changes are byte-identical in findings — prove it. Tighten, never downgrade.
2. **Align first.** Plan before consequential/security code. Decide and recommend — no option menus.
3. **Feature-branch PRs only.** Never push `main`. Rebase on `origin/main`. Bare `Closes #NNNN`. CHANGELOG `[Unreleased]` in the same PR for user-visible change. Signed commits. Merging/releasing are the maintainer's.
4. **Security subtree.** Changes under `src/stayawake/bots/security/**` need the approach agreed before the PR, extra checks, and a draft PR until an adversarial round comes back clean.
5. **Adversarial verify.** Parallel refuters, lens matched to the risk, re-verify until clean. Two rounds have never been enough.
6. **Layers.** `utils → lib → core → bots → cli`. Import down-only. `test_layering` enforces it.
7. **Offline & trust.** Accurate with zero flags. Only `-x/--external` leaves the sandbox. Allowlist is operator-owned. Fail closed.
8. **Engineering.** Value before coverage. Measure before optimizing. Reuse before building. Right depth. Self-documenting names. Never comment a variable — fix the name.

Tests are the spec. Never delete one to go green. Mutate the pin. Public surfaces say what a user observes.
